From: pi-286-games maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] bios: omit the PNG logo path when libpng is disabled

The appliance disables screenshots and libpng to avoid carrying an unused
image stack. The optional BIOS startup logo decoder was not guarded by
C_LIBPNG, which leaves PNG types and embedded logo symbols referenced in a
libpng-free build. Keep the text splash while compiling out only that decoder.

---
 src/ints/bios.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ints/bios.cpp b/src/ints/bios.cpp
index 645878b..0000000 100644
--- a/src/ints/bios.cpp
+++ b/src/ints/bios.cpp
@@ -11017,6 +11017,7 @@ startfunction:
 
         BIOS_Int10RightJustifiedPrint(x,y,msg);
 
+        #if C_LIBPNG
         {
             png_bytep rows[1];
             unsigned char *row = NULL;/*png_width*/
@@ -11162,6 +11163,7 @@ startfunction:
             if (png_fp) fclose(png_fp);
         }
 
+        #endif
         if (machine == MCH_PC98 && textsplash) {
             unsigned int bo, lastline = 7;
             for (unsigned int i=0; i<=lastline; i++) {
